./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:7:> **ABSTRACT**: `scx_cake` is an experimental BPF CPU scheduler that adapts the network [CAKE](https://www.bufferbloat.net/projects/codel/wiki/Cake/) algorithm's DRR++ (Deficit Round Robin++) for CPU scheduling. Designed for **gaming workloads** on modern AMD and Intel hardware.
./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:19:> This scheduler is experimental and intended for use with `sched_ext` on Linux Kernel 6.12+. Performance may vary depending on hardware and user configuration.
./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:44:# Prerequisites: Linux Kernel 6.12+ with sched_ext, Rust toolchain
