./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:262:3. **Preempt decision**: If `elapsed >= vprot_ns` → `scx_bpf_kick_cpu(victim, SCX_KICK_PREEMPT)`. Otherwise → suppressed (counted as `nr_vprot_suppressed` in stats).
./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:275:The clock domain fix in `cake_running` (using `scx_bpf_now()` instead of `p->se.exec_start`) prevents a subtle starvation bug: after ~22 minutes, accumulated IRQ time drift in `exec_start` would exceed the u32 wrap boundary, corrupting elapsed-time checks and causing unconditional preemption (priority inversion).
