docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2583:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:1:# scx_cake: CAKE DRR++ Adapted for CPU Scheduling
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2584:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:5:[![Status: Experimental](https://img.shields.io/badge/Status-Experimental-orange.svg?style=flat-square)](https://github.com/sched-ext/scx)
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2585:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:7:> **ABSTRACT**: `scx_cake` is an experimental BPF CPU scheduler that adapts the network [CAKE](https://www.bufferbloat.net/projects/codel/wiki/Cake/) algorithm's DRR++ (Deficit Round Robin++) for CPU scheduling. Designed for **gaming workloads** on modern AMD and Intel hardware.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2586:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:19:> This scheduler is experimental and intended for use with `sched_ext` on Linux Kernel 6.12+. Performance may vary depending on hardware and user configuration.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2587:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:44:# Prerequisites: Linux Kernel 6.12+ with sched_ext, Rust toolchain
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2588:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:47:git clone https://github.com/sched-ext/scx.git
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2589:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:48:cd scx && cargo build --release -p scx_cake
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2590:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:51:sudo ./target/release/scx_cake
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2591:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:54:sudo scx_cake -v
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2592:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:61:Traditional schedulers (CFS, EEVDF) optimize for **fairness** — if a game and a compiler both run, each gets 50% CPU time. For gaming, this creates two problems:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2593:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:66:**scx_cake's answer**: Detect the game process family automatically (Steam, Wine/Proton, native games) and give it scheduling priority. Non-game tasks are classified by PELT CPU utilization into NORMAL, HOG, or BG classes with progressively lower priority. The system self-tunes — no manual configuration needed.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2594:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:68:This is the same insight behind network CAKE: short flows (DNS, gaming packets) should not be delayed by bulk flows (downloads). scx_cake applies this to CPU time.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2595:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:74:`scx_cake` classifies every task into one of four classes. Classification uses PELT (Per-Entity Load Tracking) utilization from the kernel and automatic game family detection via process tree analysis.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2596:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:91:2. **PELT-based classification**: Every 64th stop, the scheduler reads the kernel's `util_avg` for each task. Tasks with ≥78% CPU utilization are classified as HOG; lower-utilization non-game tasks become BG during GAMING state, or NORMAL otherwise.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2597:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:139:scx_cake uses a virtual runtime system inspired by EEVDF:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2598:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:142:- **Nice scaling**: Per-task `nice_shift` (0-12) scales runtime cost. High `nice` priority → less vruntime cost → dispatches sooner. Computed once per 64 stops from `p->scx.weight`.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2599:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:155:        SELECT["cake_select_cpu<br/>3-gate + tunnel"] --> |GATE 1| PREV["prev_cpu idle?<br/>scx_bpf_test_and_clear_cpu_idle"]
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2600:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:157:        SELECT --> |GATE 3| KERNEL["scx_bpf_select_cpu_dfl<br/>kernel authoritative idle scan"]
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2601:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:160:        PREV --> LOCALON["SCX_DSQ_LOCAL_ON<br/>direct to CPU"]
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2602:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:166:        DISPATCH --> |"1. Local LLC<br/>scx_bpf_dsq_move_to_local"| LOCAL["Run task"]
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2603:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:239:| Anti-pattern                | scx_cake                                      |
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2604:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:249:`select_cpu` caches `scx_bpf_now()` in per-CPU BSS (`cpu_bss[cpu].cached_now`). `enqueue` reuses this value, saving ~15ns (1 kfunc trampoline entry) on the all-busy path.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2605:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:262:3. **Preempt decision**: If `elapsed >= vprot_ns` → `scx_bpf_kick_cpu(victim, SCX_KICK_PREEMPT)`. Otherwise → suppressed (counted as `nr_vprot_suppressed` in stats).
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2606:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:275:The clock domain fix in `cake_running` (using `scx_bpf_now()` instead of `p->se.exec_start`) prevents a subtle starvation bug: after ~22 minutes, accumulated IRQ time drift in `exec_start` would exceed the u32 wrap boundary, corrupting elapsed-time checks and causing unconditional preemption (priority inversion).
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2607:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:347:1. **Warmup**: 1 second pause for the scheduler to stabilize
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2608:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:359:The scheduler exits automatically after printing. Requires a **debug build** (release builds silently ignore `--testing`). Useful for comparing scheduling throughput across code changes.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2609:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:363:Instead of per-tier multipliers, scx_cake uses a **yield-gated quantum** system:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2610:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:377:sudo scx_cake
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2611:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:380:sudo scx_cake -p esports
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2612:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:383:sudo scx_cake --quantum 1500 -v
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2613:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:386:sudo scx_cake -p battery
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2614:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:393:`scx_cake` has two build modes that control whether telemetry instrumentation is compiled into the BPF code.
