docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3049:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:7:`scx_chaos` is a specialized scheduler that intentionally introduces various forms of latency and performance degradation to help expose race conditions and timing-dependent bugs in applications. Unlike traditional schedulers that aim for optimal performance, `scx_chaos` is designed to stress-test applications by introducing controlled chaos into the scheduling process.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3050:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:13:The scheduler supports several "chaos traits" that can be enabled individually or in combination, with more to come:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3051:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:44:Run without chaos features (baseline performance):
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3052:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:47:sudo scx_chaos
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3053:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:53:sudo scx_chaos --random-delay-frequency 0.1 --random-delay-min-us 100 --random-delay-max-us 1000
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3054:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:59:sudo scx_chaos --cpufreq-frequency 0.2 --cpufreq-min 400000 --cpufreq-max 2000000
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3055:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:65:sudo scx_chaos --degradation-frequency 0.15 --degradation-frac7 64
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3056:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:71:sudo scx_chaos --kprobes-for-random-delays schedule do_exit --kprobe-random-delay-frequency 0.05 --kprobe-random-delay-min-us 50 --kprobe-random-delay-max-us 500
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3057:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:76:Run a specific command under the chaos scheduler:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3058:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:79:sudo scx_chaos [chaos-options] -- ./your-application --app-args
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3059:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:86:Focus chaos on a specific process and its children:
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3060:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:89:sudo scx_chaos --pid 1234 [chaos-options]
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3061:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:97:sudo scx_chaos --stats 1.0 [chaos-options]  # Update every 1 second
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3062:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:103:sudo scx_chaos --monitor 2.0
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3063:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:112:sudo scx_chaos --repeat-failure [chaos-options] -- ./test-app
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3064:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:115:sudo scx_chaos --repeat-success [chaos-options] -- ./test-app
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3065:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:120:> **Note:** For the most up-to-date and complete CLI documentation, run `scx_chaos --help`. This includes all chaos-specific options as well as the full set of p2dq performance tuning options.
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3066:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:151:- `--ppid-targeting`: Focus on target process and children (default: true)
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3067:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:160:- Modern Linux kernel with `sched_ext` support, chaos has very limited backward compatibility
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3068:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:168:- **CI/CD Integration**: Automated testing with controlled chaos injection
docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:3069:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:182:`scx_chaos` is built on the `sched_ext` framework and uses the `scx_p2dq` scheduler as its base. It implements chaos traits through BPF programs that intercept scheduling decisions and apply configured disruptions based on probability distributions.
